      "content": "The thing is, the new model is significantly smaller. It's basically a distillation. We're worried that the loss of the complex predictive layers in your current architecture might lead to a drop in accuracy for the more nuanced protein-ligand binding simulations. Basically, we're worried we might miss some of the subtle errors that could sink a trial later on. Any thoughts on that?",
